\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces t-SNE of penultimate features on pooled KIMORE, REHAB246, and UI-PRMD sequences, for the scratch TCN (top) and ST-GCN (bottom). \textbf  {Left:} colored by acquisition sensor --- the three corpora form cleanly separated clusters for both backbones, the visual counterpart of the perfect ($1.00$) sensor-identity probe. \textbf  {Right:} the same embedding with target repetitions colored by correctness label (KIMORE, in grey, has no binary label); correct and incorrect repetitions are intermixed within each sensor cluster. The encoders organize features by sensor, not by movement quality.}}{6}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:embedding-tsne}{{1}{6}{t-SNE of penultimate features on pooled KIMORE, REHAB246, and UI-PRMD sequences, for the scratch TCN (top) and ST-GCN (bottom). \textbf {Left:} colored by acquisition sensor --- the three corpora form cleanly separated clusters for both backbones, the visual counterpart of the perfect ($1.00$) sensor-identity probe. \textbf {Right:} the same embedding with target repetitions colored by correctness label (KIMORE, in grey, has no binary label); correct and incorrect repetitions are intermixed within each sensor cluster. The encoders organize features by sensor, not by movement quality}{figure.1}{}}
